EXT. BOCCE COURT - COMMUNITY CLUB - DUSK

Crushed oyster shell, rolled flat. String lights. Folding chairs along the rail. Final match, tied.

NONNO ALDO BARSANTI (80s, cardigan, one eye clouded) crouches at the foul line. His partner LUCIA FERRANTE (70s, sun hat, fierce) stands beside him. Across the court: the DONOVAN BROTHERS, PADRAIC (50s, mustache) and CORMAC (50s, mustache, identical), arms crossed. Between them, REFEREE SIGNORA TESTA (60s, whistle, a ruler in her hand) measures the gap between pallino and ball. In the front row, young KOFI ANTWI (10, orange soda, the only one not wearing white) watches.

Aldo rolls. The ball curves, kisses the pallino, stops.

LUCIA
Eh!

PADRAIC
That's a touch.

CORMAC
That's a foul.

TESTA
(measuring)
Touch. Aldo's.

CORMAC
Madonna.

Cormac hurls his ball. It cracks into Lucia's, scattering the cluster. Lucia lunges. Padraic grabs her arm. Aldo grabs Padraic's collar. Testa blows the whistle, step-stepping between them with the ruler held like a sword, and Kofi stands on his chair, soda raised, and the entire club goes silent as the pallino rolls to a stop at the exact center of the court.
